  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it in a browser, so the rendering and motion are untested. The scene loads `/assets/soldier.glb` through `defineModelAssets`, using the sha256 from the docs recipe. The soldier is scaled to 1.8 m and starts on the `Walk` loop. Each frame it moves around a radius-4 circle at the origin and turns to face its direction of travel, assuming the model's forward axis is +Z. Pressing `r` plays `Run` with a 0.4 s crossfade and `w` goes back to `Walk`. Speed eases between 1.4 and 3.6 m/s over the same time. The ground is a 30×30 plane, lit by a neutral environment, a hemisphere light and a shadow-casting directional light. A fixed perspective camera looks down at the whole circle, so the soldier stays in frame. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first frame callback.",
